---
description: Shell script safety (scoped to .sh/.bash/.zsh)
globs: ["**/*.sh", "**/*.bash", "**/*.zsh"]
alwaysApply: false
---

# Shell scripts

- `#!/usr/bin/env bash` + `set -euo pipefail`; `IFS=$'\n\t'` when iterating.
- Quote every expansion (`"$var"`, `"${arr[@]}"`); use arrays for command args, never `eval`.
- `mktemp` for temp files with `trap 'rm -rf "$TMP"' EXIT`.
- Check binaries with `command -v` before use; fail with a clear message.
- No secrets in scripts or `ps`-visible args; read from env or stdin.
- Prefer `--` before positional paths; `rm -rf` only on validated, non-empty variables.
- Run `shellcheck` when available; skill: `bash-defensive-patterns`.
